From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Goyvaerts <jonathan.goyvaerts@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 11:49:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] soc: apple: clpc: Add the T6040 demand table

The T6040 (M4 Pro) has DCS states 0-5 on PMC rail 0 and fabric states
0-2 on rail 1. macOS writes the CLPC agent's floor word as
MEM | SOC << 4 from the cluster performance levels, through a mapping
it receives from user space, so this table is measured, like the T8140
one.

A busy cluster in the upper half of its frequency range asks for DCS 5
and fabric 2. With that floor held the CPUs reach 237-242 GB/s at
135 ns DRAM latency, against 41 GB/s and 314 ns at the lowest states
(macOS on the same machine: 248 GB/s, 121 ns). The DCS returns to its
lowest state within 40 ms of the floor being dropped.

No cluster runs below a quarter of its maximum, so the first column
only completes the table. The second column (DCS 2, fabric 1) is
provisional until the power of each DCS state is measured.

Signed-off-by: Jonathan Goyvaerts <jonathan.goyvaerts@gmail.com>
Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 drivers/soc/apple/clpc.c | 18 ++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/apple/clpc.c b/drivers/soc/apple/clpc.c
index 382dc669b5..ac38b3980b 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/apple/clpc.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/apple/clpc.c
@@ -609,9 +609,27 @@ static const struct apple_clpc_hw apple_clpc_hw_t8140 = {
 	.pmp_agent = 0,
 };
 
+/*
+ * T6040: DCS states 0-5 on rail 0, fabric states 0-2 on rail 1. No cluster
+ * runs below a quarter of its maximum (P 1260 of 4512 MHz, E 1020 of
+ * 2592 MHz), so the first column only completes the table. A busy cluster
+ * in the upper half asks for the top states. With the floor held at DCS 5
+ * and fabric 2 the CPUs read 237-242 GB/s at 135 ns DRAM latency, against
+ * 41 GB/s and 314 ns at 0 and 0. The second column is provisional until the
+ * power of each DCS state is measured.
+ */
+static const struct apple_clpc_hw apple_clpc_hw_t6040 = {
+	.rail = { [APPLE_CLPC_DCS] = 0, [APPLE_CLPC_SOC] = 1 },
+	.map = {
+		[APPLE_CLPC_DCS] = { 1, 2, 5, 5 },
+		[APPLE_CLPC_SOC] = { 0, 1, 2, 2 },
+	},
+};
+
 static const struct of_device_id apple_clpc_of_match[] = {
 	{ .compatible = "apple,t8132-clpc", .data = &apple_clpc_hw_t8132 },
 	{ .compatible = "apple,t8140-clpc", .data = &apple_clpc_hw_t8140 },
+	{ .compatible = "apple,t6041-clpc", .data = &apple_clpc_hw_t6040 },
 	{}
 };
 MODULE_DEVICE_TABLE(of, apple_clpc_of_match);
